# A cube with 24 vertices and 24 texcoords, so every geometric corner appears in
# three faces with three different UVs.
#
# This is the case that pins ObjUtils.makeTexCoordsUnique. The reference
# implementation keeps one "used texcoord" slot per *vertex index*: the first face
# to touch a vertex pins its texcoord, and any later face that needs a different
# texcoord for the same vertex forks a copy of the vertex. Because the vertex
# buffer is uploaded in the order that produces, a different fork order shows up
# as a byte difference even when the rendered cube is identical.
#
# Vertex layout, so the seam structure is readable:
#   1-4   z = -0.5 face, UVs of the -Z side
#   5-8   z = +0.5 face, UVs of the +Z side
#   9-12  y = -0.5 face, UVs of the -Y side
#   13-16 y = +0.5 face, UVs of the +Y side
#   17-20 x = -0.5 face, UVs of the -X side
#   21-24 x = +0.5 face, UVs of the +X side

v -0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v  0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v  0.5  0.5 -0.5
v -0.5  0.5 -0.5

v -0.5 -0.5  0.5
v  0.5 -0.5  0.5
v  0.5  0.5  0.5
v -0.5  0.5  0.5

v -0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v  0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v  0.5 -0.5  0.5
v -0.5 -0.5  0.5

v -0.5  0.5 -0.5
v  0.5  0.5 -0.5
v  0.5  0.5  0.5
v -0.5  0.5  0.5

v -0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v -0.5  0.5 -0.5
v -0.5  0.5  0.5
v -0.5 -0.5  0.5

v  0.5 -0.5 -0.5
v  0.5  0.5 -0.5
v  0.5  0.5  0.5
v  0.5 -0.5  0.5

# Six distinct UV rectangles, 0.0-0.25, 0.25-0.5, ..., so no two faces share UVs.
vt 0.00 0.00
vt 0.25 0.00
vt 0.25 0.25
vt 0.00 0.25

vt 0.25 0.00
vt 0.50 0.00
vt 0.50 0.25
vt 0.25 0.25

vt 0.50 0.00
vt 0.75 0.00
vt 0.75 0.25
vt 0.50 0.25

vt 0.75 0.00
vt 1.00 0.00
vt 1.00 0.25
vt 0.75 0.25

vt 0.00 0.25
vt 0.25 0.25
vt 0.25 0.50
vt 0.00 0.50

vt 0.25 0.25
vt 0.50 0.25
vt 0.50 0.50
vt 0.25 0.50

usemtl cube

# -Z
f 1/1 2/2 3/3 4/4
# +Z
f 8/5 7/6 6/7 5/8
# -Y
f 9/9 10/10 11/11 12/12
# +Y
f 16/13 15/14 14/15 13/16
# -X
f 17/17 18/18 19/19 20/20
# +X
f 24/21 23/22 22/23 21/24
